{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"CodeGraph emits value-reference edges so impact analysis can catch non-call dependencies like “change this shared constant/config/lookup table, break the functions that read it,” which otherwise looked like nothing depended on the value at all; the recorded rationale I relied on is [`CHANGELOG.md` 0.10.3](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md). It keeps them precise by limiting this to constant-reader relationships without adding new nodes, and by skipping bundled/minified files plus ambiguously shadowed names so it does not guess when a read could resolve to multiple values."}}
